/**************************************************************************//**
 *
 * @file code-offsets.h
 *
 * @author Christopher A. Bohn
 *
 * @brief Named constants for unhelpful assembly language instructions.
 *
 * These instructions exist only to vary functions' addresses from student to
 *      student. If the instruction pointer / program counter reaches any
 *      code generated by these named constants, the best possible outcome will
 *      be unhelpful data being placed into a register (A64's
 *      `PADDING_004_BYTES` and T32's `PADDING_002_BYTES`). The more-likely
 *      outcome will be a segmentation fault. Which is to say, this padding will
 *      not serve as a NOP sled.
 *
 ******************************************************************************/

